WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
Also this morning, the City of Lexington is offering a new way to experience history with your family.

2
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:10.000
It's a new virtual reality experience and it transports you back into the days of the revolution.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.120
City officials say that the high-tech help offers a unique way to keep the community's rich history alive.

4
00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.520
Seven's Rob Way has the story this morning.

5
00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:23.060
An otherworldly experience bridging Lexington's past with the present.

6
00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:27.860
The iREV mixed reality tour taking place at the Lexington Visitor Center on Mass Ave.

7
00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:33.460
the virtual experience bringing people all the way back to the 1770s to interact with the past

8
00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:40.260
in a brand new way. We are so fortunate to be in a town with such consequential and fascinating

9
00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:47.220
stories to tell. We always feel the responsibility of that history with the opportunity to tell it

10
00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:52.500
in exciting and new ways. Previews of the iREV headset allowed users to explore buildings on

11
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:56.300
the Lexington Battle Green, as they were in 1775.

12
00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.060
The very place where the opening shots

13
00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.780
of the battles of Lexington and Concord

14
00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.620
rang out on April 19th,

15
00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.820
kicking off the Revolutionary War.

16
00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:06.980
They are not a replacement for being there.

17
00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:11.220
They enhance it by allowing history to step into spaces

18
00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:13.300
they otherwise could not access.

19
00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:16.100
The 20-minute tour, led by a guide in colonial dress,

20
00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.340
takes users to models of either the Meeting House

21
00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:21.180
or the Belfry, landmarks — buildings that were crucial

22
00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.040
for the people of Lexington on the morning

23
00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.200
the American Revolution began.

24
00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.680
Grandparents putting on this headset with grandchildren.

25
00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:32.000
We had people of all ages, different backgrounds.

26
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.720
Everybody understood that this is something new,

27
00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:36.080
this is something different.

28
00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:39.180
This is not another virtual reality project.

29
00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:41.320
Travel and tourism experts say the experience

30
00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:43.600
is not only a milestone for virtual reality,

31
00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.240
but for Lexington's past and future.

32
00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:50.200
This is an economic development tool.

33
00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:53.700
people will come just for this experience and they will talk about it.

34
00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:58.660
The moment you you put this on you are transported to another time and when

35
00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:03.160
you're picking up things that existed hundreds of years ago it's it's an

36
00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:08.160
experience that I welcome everyone to have and really enjoy. You can book an

37
00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:12.280
iREV tour on the Lexington Visitors Center website. In the newsroom, Rob Way,

38
00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:15.800
7News Today in New England.
